  "historical_output_text": " In a dim, sunless day I found comfort as familiar sounds carried from their familiar noontides in a small, urban community where we walked through cobbling roads where children were seen rolling and racing toy bikes on either street, but it all felt strange in an oddly comforting familiarity that seemed more distant with passing moments.\n\nWe arrived to visit family as always for their Sunday gatherings where everyone knew and spoke each name like the streets where each of the shops on either ends carried unique and specific goods to be shared as they spoke. Yet this place had become something less tangible; like it once held my past in every moment but no present could exist",
